WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.870
You're on a train,
looking out of the window.

2
00:00:02.920 --> 00:00:07.350
Another train, going the same
way, slides slowly past you.

3
00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:10.850
But someone standing on the
platform sees that same train rush

4
00:00:10.900 --> 00:00:11.830
by.

5
00:00:11.880 --> 00:00:14.270
So how fast is it really going?

6
00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:16.090
It depends who you ask.

7
00:00:16.140 --> 00:00:18.610
In this mission, you'll measure speed:

8
00:00:18.660 --> 00:00:21.630
how much distance something
covers each second.

9
00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:24.470
You'll turn journeys into
distance-time graphs,

10
00:00:24.520 --> 00:00:26.950
where a steeper line means faster.

11
00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:30.210
Then you'll compare speeds
from different points of view:

12
00:00:30.260 --> 00:00:32.510
the platform, and the train.

13
00:00:32.560 --> 00:00:36.660
Your mission: work out how
fast the other train is going.
